From 9bcac8c06c876dfa13aa6d05cb14a9402bba6726 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 08:27:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] test(corpus): traces and goldens for the 2025-11-25
 utilities pages

Three conforming stdio sessions (`stdio-progress`, `stdio-task-progress`,
`stdio-cancellation`) carry the pass path of every judged clause, in both
directions, including the answer that crosses its cancellation on the wire and
the task whose token outlives its `CreateTaskResult`. Twelve violation traces,
one per check, each failing exactly the clause it is named for: the two shapes
the dogfood found judged clean (`prog-013-progress-token-never-issued`,
`canc-018-cancellation-of-unknown-request`) among them.

The golden diff is the one ADR-0013 predicts for clauses entering a revision:
every 2025-11-25 golden moves `totals.excluded` 232 -> 246 and gains the 13
judged rows (not observed, or pass where the session pinged), the exclusion
ledger gains 14 rows, and the nine HTML goldens re-render. No existing row's
outcome moved. The provenance ledger gains a row per trace and its accounting
table is recounted (119 goldens, 246 ledger rows, 84 distinct not-observed sets).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
